# Story 12.6 live-validation artifacts.
#
# What is committed: everything a reader needs to re-derive a number — the drivers
# (`run_after.py` for the scenario chain, `run_after_tts.py` for the speech), the two
# JSON dumps they produce (`after_scenes.json`, `after_durations.json`), the reports
# measured off them (`after.json`, `baseline.json`) and the prose that reads them
# (`after.md`, `baseline.md`, `seeding.md`). All of it is text; the whole committed
# payload is well under a megabyte.
#
# What is ignored: `tts_audio/` — the eight WAVs `run_after_tts.py` synthesizes to get
# AC8's WPM (~8 MB). No claim in this story rests on anyone listening to one: the only
# thing read off them is duration, and that duration is already in
# `after_durations.json`. They are regenerable by re-running `run_after_tts.py` against
# the same `after_scenes.json` — expect the seconds to move by ~0.2 % between runs (two
# measured samples: 169.23 s / 168.93 s), which is the TTS's own variance and is
# recorded in `after.md`.
#
# Nothing here is the only surviving copy of anything.

tts_audio/

# Listening copies, made on request for a human ear rather than for a number:
# the eight scenes concatenated into one track, and the same script as plain text.
# Both are regenerable — the mp3 by `ffmpeg -f concat` over `tts_audio/`, the text
# straight out of `after_scenes.json`. No measurement rests on either.
12-6-after-narration.mp3
12-6-after-narration.txt

# The prompt ablation (`ablation.md`) adds two more arms on the same SCP, and the same
# split applies to them: the scenes dumps, the durations, the measurement reports, the
# rendered-prompt receipts and the drivers (`run_ablation.py`, `count_devices.py`,
# `make_listening_copy.py`) are committed — every number in `ablation.md` is re-derivable
# from them — while the listening copies are not. Each arm's eight WAVs land under the
# already-ignored `tts_audio/12-6-arm{A,B}/`, and the concatenated track plus its
# read-along script are rebuilt by `make_listening_copy.py` from those WAVs. Only Jay's
# ear reads them; no claim in `ablation.md` does.
12-6-armA-narration.mp3
12-6-armA-narration.txt
12-6-armB-narration.mp3
12-6-armB-narration.txt
